==Enemy==
While Chocolate Doge has low range and damage, it has a guaranteed chance to produce Lv.4 [[Mini-Wave|Mini-Waves]], which allow it to deal steady, constant damage, especially when stacked. Due to its large health pool, it can take quite the beating before dying. Also note that it cannot be permanently frozen with [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] due to its freeze immunity, leaving it to be a constant danger as long as it is left alive.

==Strategy==
Because of its Freeze Immunity, the best way to take out this delicious Doge is to kill it quickly. [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]], [[Talents|Talented]] [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]], or [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Assassin BearCat]] are perfect for the job due to their high damage against Dark enemies. While its Mini-Waves don't deal much damage, choosing to use a [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shield]] could be wise, especially if using any low health Cats like [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]], most [[Tales of the Nekoluga (Gacha Event)|Lugas]] or [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]]. Any Wave Shield should work well for the job, as Chocolate Doge has lower range than even [[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Supercat]] and [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]]. At higher magnifications, it is also recommended to utilize units with [[Long Distance]]; since this durable delicacy primarily serves as a meatshield for troublesome midrange and backline enemies, its high health and slow speed can be used to your advantage as a springboard for your own cats.

